== 2026-09-14 note (hc2): two of the five re-runs above are VOID and are run again below.
   "time" (13:38:46Z): the break itself was broken. The replaced text ended before " catch { return null; }", so the added
   "// NEGATIVE CONTROL (b)" comment commented out the catch; the copy's queue.js did not parse and the page never loaded
   (red at "visit-name not found" plus page errors, not at the original-time assertion). The comment is now /* */.
   "queue" (13:36:36Z): red was caused by the break (the check-in was erased on its first failed send, so its tasks never
   showed) but only as a 120 s timeout. offline.spec's 500-once test now asserts "1 saved on this phone" right after the first
   failed send, and tap() scrolls with a 10 s limit, so the red names the lost event.
   "board", "familynote" and "overlay" (13:39Z) stand: unbroken copy passed, broken copy red at the targeted assertion.

